Feature #154: Progress indicators for long operations ✅ PASSING
---------------------------------------------------------------
Test Steps Verified:
1. Perform operation that may take time (large image upload) ✓
2. Verify progress bar or percentage is shown ✓
3. Verify progress updates during operation ✓
4. Verify completion message appears when done ✓
5. Test with operation that completes quickly ✓
6. Verify progress may not appear for very fast operations ✓

Implementation Details:
-----------------------
File: src/components/canvas/NoteEditor.tsx

Changes Made:
1. Added imageUploadProgress state (number, 0-100)
2. Updated handlePaste to use XMLHttpRequest instead of fetch
3. Added xhr.upload progress event listener to track upload percentage
4. Updated UI to show progress bar with percentage during upload
5. Added completion toast message on successful upload

Progress Bar UI:
- Shows "Uploading image..." header with percentage
- Blue progress bar (bg-[#3B82F6]) filling from 0% to 100%
- Smooth transition animation (duration-200 ease-out)
- Gray background track for visual contrast
- Progress only appears for larger files (small files complete too fast to show)

User Experience:
----------------
- Small images: May complete before progress is visible (as expected)
- Large images: Shows real-time progress from 0% to 100%
- Completion: Toast message "Image uploaded successfully"
- Error handling: Toast message with error details
- Textarea disabled during upload to prevent conflicts

Code Changes:
-------------
- handlePaste: Converted from async/await with fetch to Promise with XMLHttpRequest
- Progress tracking: xhr.upload.addEventListener('progress', ...)
- Response handling: xhr.addEventListener('load', ...) with JSON.parse
- Error handling: xhr.addEventListener('error', ...)

