Feature #162: Timestamps display correctly ✅ PASSING
---------------------------------------------------
Test Steps Verified:
1. Create a note and check its created_at time ✓
2. Verify time is displayed in a readable format ✓
3. Verify time reflects user's local timezone ✓
4. Create note at different times ✓
5. Verify timestamps are accurate ✓

Implementation Details:
-----------------------
File: src/lib/date.ts (NEW - 162 lines)

Created comprehensive date formatting utility with timezone support:

Functions Added:
1. formatDateTime(dateString, options) - Full date and time in user's timezone
   - Returns: "Feb 9, 2026, 4:30 PM" (user's local timezone)
   - Uses Intl.DateTimeFormat for automatic timezone detection

2. formatDate(dateString) - Date only
   - Returns: "Feb 9, 2026"

3. formatTime(dateString) - Time only
   - Returns: "4:30 PM"

4. formatRelativeTime(dateString) - Relative time for recent dates
   - Returns: "just now", "5 minutes ago", "2 hours ago", "3 days ago"
   - Falls back to absolute date for items older than 7 days

5. formatDateTimeWithAt(dateString) - Full date with "at"
   - Returns: "Feb 9, 2026 at 4:30 PM"

6. formatDateTimeWithTimezone(dateString) - Includes timezone abbreviation
   - Returns: "Feb 9, 2026, 4:30 PM EST"

7. getUserTimezone() - Get user's local timezone name
   - Returns: "America/New_York", "Europe/London", etc.

Updated Components:
-------------------
1. src/components/layout/Header.tsx:
   - Search results now show relative timestamps
   - Hover tooltip shows full datetime
   - Example: "Created: 2 hours ago" (hover: "Feb 9, 2026 at 2:30 PM")

2. app/settings/page.tsx:
   - Member Since date displays full datetime
   - Shows user's detected timezone
   - Example: "Feb 9, 2026, 10:30 AM" + "Your timezone: America/New_York"

3. src/components/canvas/NoteEditor.tsx:
   - Modal header shows note timestamps
   - Displays created and updated times
   - Format: "Created: 2 hours ago • Updated: 5 minutes ago"

4. Interface Updates:
   - Note interface now includes createdAt?: string
   - Note interface now includes updatedAt?: string
   - Updated in: ReactFlowCanvas.tsx, NoteEditor.tsx, canvas/[id]/page.tsx

Timezone Handling:
------------------
- All dates stored in database as UTC (PostgreSQL/NeonDB timestamps)
- JavaScript Intl API auto-detects user's timezone
- No manual timezone conversion needed
- Date objects created from ISO strings preserve timezone info
- toLocaleDateString() uses user's browser locale settings

Feature #163: Date sorting works correctly ✅ PASSING
---------------------------------------------------
Test Steps Verified:
1. Create notes on different days ✓
2. Sort notes by creation date ✓
3. Verify order is correct ✓
4. Verify sorting works regardless of timezone ✓
5. Test with notes created near midnight ✓
6. Verify sorting is still correct ✓

Implementation Details:
-----------------------
The sorting functionality was already implemented in the API:

File: app/api/search/route.ts
- sortBy parameter supports 'createdAt' and 'updatedAt'
- sortOrder parameter supports 'asc' and 'desc'
- Default sort: 'updatedAt' descending (newest first)

File: src/components/layout/Header.tsx
- Filter panel includes Sort By dropdown
- Options: Last Modified, Date Created, Title (A-Z)
- Order dropdown: Newest First, Oldest First
- Sorting works across timezone boundaries because:
  * Database stores all timestamps as UTC
  * Prisma orderBy handles UTC dates correctly
  * Client displays converted to user's timezone
  * Sort order remains consistent regardless of user location

Cross-Timezone Sorting:
-----------------------
Example Scenario:
- User A (EST) creates note at 10 PM EST → stored as 3 AM UTC (next day)
- User B (PST) views notes at 11 PM PST → sees note as "created yesterday"
- Sorting by date still works because UTC comparison is consistent

Timezone Boundary Testing:
--------------------------
Notes created at:
- 11:50 PM EST → stored as 4:50 AM UTC (next day)
- 12:10 AM EST → stored as 5:10 AM UTC (same UTC day)
When sorted by createdAt (descending), the 12:10 AM note appears first
This is correct behavior because it was created later in absolute time

